From: Code and Solder <codeandsolder@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] pstore: use vendor-compatible QCN ftrace zone signature for diagnosis

The recovery kernel is 32-bit Linux 5.4.213. A Linux 6.18 ftrace PRZ
signature is rejected on vendor reboot and its header is reset, losing
the only persistent instruction history. Use the vendor version salt
only for the ftrace zone. The original console and oops buffers are
unchanged. Deliberately diagnostic-only; revert after bring-up.

Signed-off-by: Code and Solder <codeandsolder@gmail.com>
---
--- a/fs/pstore/ram.c
+++ b/fs/pstore/ram.c
@@ -805,11 +805,18 @@
 	cxt->max_ftrace_cnt = (cxt->flags & RAMOOPS_FLAG_FTRACE_PER_CPU)
 				? nr_cpu_ids
 				: 1;
 	err = ramoops_init_przs("ftrace", dev, cxt, &cxt->fprzs, &paddr,
 				cxt->ftrace_size, -1,
-				&cxt->max_ftrace_cnt, LINUX_VERSION_CODE,
+				&cxt->max_ftrace_cnt,
+				/* Keep the recovered ftrace ring readable by the
+				 * stock Acer Linux 5.4.213 ramoops driver.
+				 * Without a shared PRZ signature its initialization
+				 * resets the ring before any userspace capture.
+				 * Diagnostic only: preserve all other pstore zones.
+				 */
+				KERNEL_VERSION(5, 4, 213),
 				(cxt->flags & RAMOOPS_FLAG_FTRACE_PER_CPU)
 					? PRZ_FLAG_NO_LOCK : 0);
 	if (err)
 		goto fail_init;
 
